From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z5vix <z5vix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:55:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Xbox app: IPackageManager3, both Gaming Services identity layouts, stand-in package updates

Applies after 0002. Found bringing up the current Xbox app (XboxPcApp / XboxPcAppFT):
- appxdeploymentclient: IPackageManager3 (the volume methods; the volume is package_volume_create's system
  volume). The app's full-trust helper used the NULL that E_NOINTERFACE left it and crashed at start.
- winexboxauth: IUser and IXboxAuthManager keep their name-derived IIDs while Gaming Services inserts methods
  (User.LocalId, NonRoamableId, GetMsaTicketWithUiAsync; XboxAuthManager.RestartApps), so the vtable an app calls
  depends on the Microsoft.GamePlatform.Services.winmd its projection was built from. The previous table matched
  neither the Microsoft Store's winmd nor the Xbox app's: the Xbox app read User.AgeGroup (3) as XuidStr's HSTRING
  and faulted on address 0x13 in two processes. Both layouts are kept now, chosen by whether the package's own
  winmd declares get_LocalId / RestartApps; the statics gain SetSandbox, IsValidSandboxName, SignOutAllUsersAsync.
- appxdeploymentclient: AddPackageAsync / AddPackageToVolumeAsync for stand-in packages. The Xbox app updates
  Gaming Services from the gamingservices-signed.appxbundle it carries when the installed version is older (it
  ships 39.118; the stand-in said 37.114) and showed "Try the update again" (0x80004001). The package's identity
  is read from its manifest (zip / zip64); when it is a stand-in, the stand-in is raised to that version and the
  deployment completes. Other packages are still not deployed from here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
